content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-110 – AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-24020",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 92 C and rising. The manufacturer limits are: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C. The reading is above the trip limit, so the pump must be stopped. The limits apply to housing-surface measurement, which is how this reading was taken.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bearing temperature is above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit. Site standard SSP-07 therefore requires a priority-1 work order to be raised within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 4.0 mm/s. This falls in Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation') of HF-300 Figure 3. It is below the Zone C boundary (4.5) and well below Zone D (7.1, 'Damage likely – stop the pump'). The SSP-07 vibration stop rule (highest severity zone) is not triggered by vibration alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The drive-end bearing is audibly noisy. The manual requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature. Both conditions are present.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear or failure of the drive-end bearing (6312-C3). This is the most likely cause, given the noise combined with high temperature. It is listed as a cause of high bearing temperature and of high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing of the bearing. This is listed as a cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment between pump and motor. This is listed as a cause of high bearing temperature and of vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop pump P-110 immediately: the bearing temperature of 92 C exceeds the 90 C trip limit. Confirm the shutdown and raise/record this as a P1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC. Close and lock the suction and discharge valves. Obtain a line-break permit, then drain and vent the pump before opening it.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before dismantling, check the bearing grease quantity for over-greasing as directed by the troubleshooting table. Record the findings.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Prepare and get sign-off on a lifting plan from the shift supervisor. Use certified lifting equipment. Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg); the casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15",
        "C01",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair: drive-end HF3-512 (6312-C3) and non-drive-end HF3-510 (6310-C3). Inspect the shaft (HF3-300) and impeller for damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the impeller is removed, refit the impeller nut (M24) to 160 Nm. Tighten the bearing housing bolts (M12) to 85 Nm. All Table 5 torques are for lightly oiled threads.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only if the mechanical seal is disturbed: do NOT refit or fit HF3-450. Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B (pre-set, no sleeve measurement needed) and tighten the gland nuts to 30 Nm. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Refit the back pull-out assembly with a new casing gasket HF3-120. Tighten the casing bolts (M16) to 210 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser-align pump to motor, since the bearing housing has been moved. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove LOTO and isolations and restart under the permit. Never run dry; confirm Plan 11 seal flush. Measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading per Figure 3; the target is Zone A/B. Monitor bearing housing temperature against the 70 C normal / 80 C alarm limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replace as pair with DE bearing)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket – replace whenever casing is opened (back pull-out removal)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal – CONTINGENCY, only if seal is disturbed; supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve – CONTINGENCY, only if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC before any work inside the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves. Line-break permit, with the pump drained and vented first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, which is over 25 kg. A lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing temperature is above the manufacturer alarm limit, so a P1 work order must be raised within the shift. The pump is stopped because the 90 C trip limit has been exceeded.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. The seal flush is Plan 11 from the pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency, only if the mechanical seal must be replaced: 4.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal part: the manual parts list (Rev D) gives component seal HF3-450. Service bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes it with cartridge seal HF3-450B for serial HF3-22000 and above. P-110 is serial HF3-24020, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies. Use HF3-450B and never HF3-450.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm, while SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Because serial HF3-24020 falls in the bulletin's range, 30 Nm applies. The bulletin changes only the gland torque, so the other Table 5 values (casing 210 Nm, impeller nut 160 Nm, bearing housing 85 Nm) still apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop criteria: site standard SSP-07 requires an immediate stop only for vibration in the highest zone. For bearing temperature above alarm it requires only a P1 work order. The manufacturer's table sets a 90 C trip limit. At 92 C the more restrictive manufacturer trip limit governs, so the pump is stopped even though vibration (Zone B) does not trigger the SSP-07 stop rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "The manual gives no step-by-step bearing replacement procedure, bearing fitting method (heating/press), or bearing clearances beyond the 'replace as pair' rule.",
    "The grease type, quantity and relubrication interval are not specified in the evidence, so over-greasing cannot be judged against a limit.",
    "The evidence does not say whether the mechanical seal must be removed or disturbed to replace the bearings on the back pull-out assembly. If it is disturbed, can it be reused, or must HF3-450B be fitted?",
    "Why was the pump still running at 92 C, above the 90 C trip? Is a temperature trip fitted and functional on P-110?",
    "The non-drive-end bearing temperature and the direction/location of the 4.0 mm/s vibration reading were not reported. Was it the highest reading of both housings, in RMS?",
    "Is P-110 on a chemically dosed line? If so, chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required per SSP-07.",
    "Does the reliability engineer need to be consulted before restart? SSP-07 mandates this only for vibration in Zone D, which does not apply here."
  ]
}
